; =====================================================================
; cddl.abnf
;
; VERBATIM.  This is RFC 8610's own grammar, copied unchanged.  It was
; NOT authored by this project.  Do not edit it, do not correct it, do
; not reformat it.  Defects found in it are recorded in README.md,
; never repaired here.  The companion derived file that mechanically
; dedents it for tools is cddl-dedented.derived.abnf.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; CURRENCY, added 2026-10-19 by the rfc-9682 extraction (library#39
; Tier 2).  THIS FILE IS STILL CORRECT AND IS NOT SUPERSEDED AS AN
; EXTRACTION: it is RFC 8610's grammar and remains exactly that.  What
; it is not is CURRENT CDDL.  RFC 9682 ("Updates to the Concise Data
; Definition Language (CDDL) Grammar") replaces its Appendix B with a
; 55-rule grammar: 8 rules new, 6 with a changed right-hand side, 41
; carried over unchanged, 0 dropped.
;
; The six whose right-hand side CHANGED -- read records/ietf/rfc-9682
; before building a parser from any of them:
;
;     cddl    S 1*(rule S)          ->  S *(rule S)        RELAXATION
;     type2   #6 ["." uint]         ->  ["." head-number]  RELAXATION
;                                       and adds #7 ["." head-number]
;     SCHAR   ... %x80-10FFFD       ->  ... NONASCII        RESTRICTION
;     SESC    "\" (%x20-7E/%x80-)   ->  eight named escapes RESTRICTION
;                                       plus \u{hex}        + RELAXATION
;     BCHAR   ... %x5D-10FFFD       ->  ... NONASCII        RESTRICTION
;     PCHAR   %x20-7E / %x80-10FFFD ->  %x20-7E / NONASCII  RESTRICTION
;
; TWO of the 44 side conditions in grammar-gaps.derived.txt are CLOSED
; there -- G-32 (surrogates: NONASCII = %xA0-D7FF / %xE000-10FFFD, and
; the escape path is closed too) and G-33 (unrestricted escapes).  G-31
; is half-closed (the DEL asymmetry is fixed and stated; the
; CRLF/line-spanning asymmetry stands, still unstated anywhere) and
; G-04 is amended rather than fixed.  The other 38 stand.
;
; NOT fixed by RFC 9682: the bare-LF `CRLF = %x0A / %x0D.0A` below is
; carried into RFC 9682's normative appendix BYTE-IDENTICAL, in a
; document titled *Updates to the CDDL Grammar* that rewrites PCHAR two
; lines above it and says nothing about it.
;
;   [narrowed 2026-10-19 by the rfc-9165 extraction.  An earlier draft
;   of this note said the defect "now sits in three current CDDL
;   documents", counting RFC 9165 and draft-ietf-cbor-cddl-modules
;   alongside RFC 8610.  That conflates an idiom with an error.
;   RFC 9165 §3 makes the IDENTICAL redefinition but DECLARES it, scopes
;   it exactly -- "As is customary for ABNF, the syntax of ABNF itself
;   (_not_ the syntax expressed in ABNF!) is relaxed to allow a single
;   line feed as a newline" (source lines 294-298) -- and is written by
;   one of RFC 8610's own authors.  So the SUBSTANCE is deliberate
;   community practice, and what is defective about it HERE is only that
;   it is undeclared and sits camouflaged among four core rules
;   redefined identically.  README.md's defect list is narrowed the same
;   way; the defect is real and it is a documentation defect, not a
;   grammar one.]
;
; `bsqual = "h" / "b64"` is likewise unchanged at two
; prefixes.  And none of Table 1's three disagreements with this
; grammar is resolved: RFC 9682's scope is Appendix B, Table 1 is in
; §3.11.
;
; The hazard worth knowing before trusting either grammar: the escape
; change SILENTLY DISAGREES rather than failing.  `"D\u{6f}mino"`
; parses under BOTH grammars with DIFFERENT meanings and no diagnostic
; on either side, because this file's SESC consumes backslash plus one
; character and `{`, `6`, `f`, `}` are then ordinary SCHARs.  Verified
; mechanically against both productions.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; Locator:  RFC 8610, "Concise Data Definition Language (CDDL): A
;           Notational Convention to Express Concise Binary Object
;           Representation (CBOR) and JSON Data Structures",
;           Birkholz, Vigano & Bormann, June 2019, Standards Track,
;           ISSN 2070-1721.  Appendix B, "ABNF Grammar" (Figure 13:
;           CDDL ABNF).  Source text lines 2480-2597.
;           <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8610.txt>
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full cached source text):
;   3713f2a50e23a2bea0a6147ad6c4433605a00c3d00a868bfa86a42b204997089
;
; Appendix B is NORMATIVE.  Its own preamble, quoted:
;
;      This appendix is normative.
;
;      The following is a formal definition of the CDDL syntax in ABNF
;      [RFC5234].  Note that, as is defined in ABNF, the quote-delimited
;      strings below are case insensitive (while string values and names are
;      case sensitive in CDDL).
;
; and its closing note, quoted (source lines 2601-2602):
;
;      Note that this ABNF does not attempt to reflect the detailed rules of
;      what can be in a prefixed byte string.
;
; THE RFC'S FIVE-COLUMN LEFT MARGIN IS PRESERVED on every grammar line.
; That makes this file faithful but NOT directly consumable by an ABNF
; tool: under RFC 5234 a line beginning with whitespace continues the
; previous rule, so an indented grammar collapses into one rule.  Dedent
; by exactly five columns first, or use cddl-dedented.derived.abnf.
;
; The grammar crosses two RFC page frames.  It is therefore reproduced as
; three contiguous regions (the page footer, U+000C form feed, running
; head and surrounding blank lines fall between them and are NOT
; reproduced).  No region contains any page furniture.  Concatenating
; B-1, B-2 and B-3 in order, with one blank line where each page frame
; stood, reconstructs Appendix B's grammar in full: 47 productions,
; cddl through CRLF, nothing dropped at a page break.
; =====================================================================

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM B-1 (source lines 2480-2516, sha256 6689bc055a11a5a49600a880c2a244ffc1baa1f2bd8cb499cb276897a56c89be) ----
     cddl = S 1*(rule S)
     rule = typename [genericparm] S assignt S type
          / groupname [genericparm] S assigng S grpent

     typename = id
     groupname = id

     assignt = "=" / "/="
     assigng = "=" / "//="

     genericparm = "<" S id S *("," S id S ) ">"
     genericarg = "<" S type1 S *("," S type1 S ) ">"

     type = type1 *(S "/" S type1)

     type1 = type2 [S (rangeop / ctlop) S type2]
     ; space may be needed before the operator if type2 ends in a name

     type2 = value
           / typename [genericarg]
           / "(" S type S ")"
           / "{" S group S "}"
           / "[" S group S "]"
           / "~" S typename [genericarg]
           / "&" S "(" S group S ")"
           / "&" S groupname [genericarg]
           / "#" "6" ["." uint] "(" S type S ")"
           / "#" DIGIT ["." uint]                ; major/ai
           / "#"                                 ; any

     rangeop = "..." / ".."

     ctlop = "." id

     group = grpchoice *(S "//" S grpchoice)

     grpchoice = *(grpent optcom)
; ---- END VERBATIM B-1 ----

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM B-2 (source lines 2527-2566, sha256 c03e96cff0f74fa8132e574393eb7954765ce22759e47c031c20f520bd8d2557) ----
     grpent = [occur S] [memberkey S] type
            / [occur S] groupname [genericarg]  ; preempted by above
            / [occur S] "(" S group S ")"

     memberkey = type1 S ["^" S] "=>"
               / bareword S ":"
               / value S ":"

     bareword = id

     optcom = S ["," S]

     occur = [uint] "*" [uint]
           / "+"
           / "?"

     uint = DIGIT1 *DIGIT
          / "0x" 1*HEXDIG
          / "0b" 1*BINDIG
          / "0"

     value = number
           / text
           / bytes

     int = ["-"] uint

     ; This is a float if it has fraction or exponent; int otherwise
     number = hexfloat / (int ["." fraction] ["e" exponent ])
     hexfloat = ["-"] "0x" 1*HEXDIG ["." 1*HEXDIG] "p" exponent
     fraction = 1*DIGIT
     exponent = ["+"/"-"] 1*DIGIT

     text = %x22 *SCHAR %x22
     SCHAR = %x20-21 / %x23-5B / %x5D-7E / %x80-10FFFD / SESC
     SESC = "\" (%x20-7E / %x80-10FFFD)

     bytes = [bsqual] %x27 *BCHAR %x27
     BCHAR = %x20-26 / %x28-5B / %x5D-10FFFD / SESC / CRLF
     bsqual = "h" / "b64"
; ---- END VERBATIM B-2 ----

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM B-3 (source lines 2583-2597, sha256 d3be4c27ca7e4f45f7b717aac39f5efc2ee44368043128bc94264babb1db799e) ----
     id = EALPHA *(*("-" / ".") (EALPHA / DIGIT))
     ALPHA = %x41-5A / %x61-7A
     EALPHA = ALPHA / "@" / "_" / "$"
     DIGIT = %x30-39
     DIGIT1 = %x31-39
     HEXDIG = DIGIT / "A" / "B" / "C" / "D" / "E" / "F"
     BINDIG = %x30-31

     S = *WS
     WS = SP / NL
     SP = %x20
     NL = COMMENT / CRLF
     COMMENT = ";" *PCHAR CRLF
     PCHAR = %x20-7E / %x80-10FFFD
     CRLF = %x0A / %x0D.0A
; ---- END VERBATIM B-3 ----
